sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Under the free-energy account of morphogenesis, genetic codes can be interpreted as parametrizing a generative model that predicts the signals each cell would sense in the target morphology, and epigenetic processes (signalling-dependent transcription) as the inversion of that model.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genome parametrizes a generative model; epigenesis inverts it";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Friston K, Levin M, Sengupta B, Pezzulo G, “Knowing one's place: a free-energy approach to pattern regulation”, Journal of the Royal Society, Interface (2015), doi:10.1098/rsif.2014.1383; section “Abstract”. Scope: Morphogenesis in multicellular organisms"
}
